*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
*** Title: Mediation model (Figure 1) - what accounts for the SMSD gap between IWP Employees and AROP w/o IWP?
*** Treatment W: smd_grp (1 = IWP Employees, 0 = AROP w/o IWP), outcome Y: smd (SMSD rebuilt from 13 items)
*** Confounders X (in all models): year, age, sex, household type, education, region, urbanisation and health
***   (general health, limitation, chronic illness PH020); prior history only in the longitudinal data (not here)
*** Mediators M (numbering = block number k in the code):
***   1  M1  income level      : income position inc_rel (% of poverty threshold); poverty gap = 100 - inc_rel, not added separately
***   2  M2a means-tested      : share of disposable income from social assistance/minimum income (HY060G) and housing allowances (HY070G)
***   3  M2b insurance-type    : share from unemployment (PY090G), sickness (PY120G) and disability benefits (PY130G), summed over the household
***   4  M2c family allowances : share from family/child allowances (HY050G)
***   5  M3  asset proxies     : tenure (HH021), capital income (HY090G > 0), rental income (HY040G > 0) - robustness only
***   6  M4  household         : other persons (18-64) in the household working >= 7 months, 0 / 1 / 2+
***   7  M2  total transfer share (HY020 - HY022) / HY020 - only for comparison with the earlier specification
***   8  health                : only if HEALTH_ROLE = "M"
***   Shares are in % of disposable household income (HY020); income from work and other sources is the reference. Transfer
***   amounts are gross (G variables), HY020 is net; most of these benefits are not taxed in Austria. Education allowances
***   (PY140G) are not modelled separately. Work intensity (RX040) is not used: it contains the person's own months of work.
*** Models (runs):
***   C   main     : M1 + M2a + M2b + M2c + M4          (income structure by type of transfer)
***   B   no M2    : M1 + M4                            (without income structure - closest to the post-transfer starting point)
***   AGG total M2 : M1 + M2 (total share) + M4         (earlier specification)
***   ROB assets   : M1 + M2a + M2b + M2c + M3 + M4
*** Method: KHB decomposition (Karlson, Holm & Breen 2012), implemented by hand so that contributions can be summed per block
***   a_j = coefficient of W in OLS of mediator j on W + X
***   b_j = coefficient of mediator j in the logit of Y on W + X + all M of the model (full model); c' = coefficient of W there
***   c   = coefficient of W in the logit of Y on W + X + residualised M (total effect, same scale) = c' + sum_j a_j * b_j (exact)
***   Reported: logit scale, share of the total gap (%), probability scale in pp (KHB-APE; block pp apportioned by the logit
***   shares) and in % of the predicted NEP rate; standard errors from the official khb command (Part G, delta method)
*** Parts: A setup | B mediators by group | C paths a and b per model | D ladder | E KHB per model | G standard errors (khb)
***        | G2 item-level decomposition with the main model C | H export
*** Health is a confounder (Figure 1). Set global HEALTH_ROLE to "M" to treat health as mediator (block 8) instead.
*** Input: SILC_All_Years_Adjusted.dta | Output: Mediation_log.txt, sheets Med_paths, Med_ladder, Med_KHB, Med_items in 05_Deprivation_Results.xlsx
*** Requires: khb (installed automatically from SSC if missing)
*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

